<title>SWEDEN: Atlas Copco Q1 profit falls eight pct.</title>
<headline>Atlas Copco Q1 profit falls eight pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish engineering company Atlas Copco gave the following figures for the first quarter ended March 31.</p>
<p>				     (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		    735 vs   803</p>
<p> Sales					 6,406 vs 6,034</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	    2.40 vs 2.94</p>
<p> Operating income and expense CHARGE 5,265 vs 5,658</p>
<p> Operating profit			    769 vs   748</p>
<p> Financial income and expense CREDIT    34 vs    13 CHARGE</p>
<p> Associated interest			 nil vs nil</p>
<p> Taxes					   258 vs   289</p>
<p> Minorities					6 vs     6</p>
<p> Net profit				    539 vs   440</p>
<p>NOTE -- Market forecasts for Atlas Copco had centred on an expected first quarter profit of 789 million crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1017</p>
</text>
